<details class="govuk-details">
    <summary class="govuk-details__summary">
        <span class="govuk-details__summary-text">
            How to understand these risk scores
        </span>
    </summary>
    <div class="govuk-details__text">
        <p class="govuk-body">
            A school’s risk scores are based on 19 risk indicators. These scores help identify where extra support or monitoring might be most helpful.
        </p>
        <p class="govuk-body">
            To see the specific data contributing to the risk scores for a school, click on the school's name.
        </p>
        <p class="govuk-body">
            To download all the data used to calculate the scores, or compare schools on their risk indicator values, use the download link above.
        </p>

        <h2 class="govuk-heading-s govuk-!-margin-top-6">
            Maximum possible scores
        </h2>

        <p class="govuk-body">
            The overall score (up to 25.50) is the total sum of:
        </p>
        <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
            <li>Financial risk (up to 18.00)</li>
            <li>Pupil and school risk (up to 5.50)</li>
            <li>Educational performance risk (up to 2.00)</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="govuk-body govuk-!-margin-top-4">
            @*TODO: update href once methodology page is created*@
            <a href="#" class="govuk-link govuk-link--no-visited-state">Read about how we define these risk indicators and RAG-rate the scores</a>
        </p>
    </div>
</details>
